coder v0.0.0-devel

USAGE:
  coder organizations show [flags] ["selected"|"me"|uuid|org_name]

  Show the organization. Using "selected" will show the selected organization
  from the "--org" flag. Using "me" will show all organizations you are a member
  of.

    - Show the organization selected with '--org=<org_name>', which the CLI
  uses:
  
       $ coder org show selected
  
    - List all organizations you are a member of:
  
       $ coder org show me
  
    - Show the organization named 'developers':
  
       $ coder org show developers
  
    - Show the organization with the given ID:
  
       $ coder org show 90ee1875-3db5-43b3-828e-af3687522e43

OPTIONS:
  -c, --column [id|name|display name|icon|description|created at|updated at|default|default org member roles] (default: id,name,default)
          Columns to display in table output.

      --only-id bool
          Only print the organization ID.

  -o, --output text|table|json (default: text)
          Output format.

———
Run `coder --help` for a list of global options.
